anatory text; when you decide to call the tool, emit the tool call itself.\nIf you use MOUSE, include integer row and col arguments.\nEFFICIENCY BUDGET \u2014 your score on each level is (baseline_actions / your_actions)^2, so every wasted action costs you quadratically.\nLevel 1: you have used 50 actions; a strong score needs about 39 or fewer. You are 1.3x over the target.\nIf you are not steadily making progress toward the level goal, commit to your single best hypothesis and the shortest sequence that tests it \u2014 do not exhaustively scan rows/columns or enumerate every option. Test one idea, read the result, then decide.", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}, {"label": "THINKING", "content": "The blue moved UP 6 times and RIGHT 1 time. The gameplay_changed is true for the last action (RIGHT), which means the blue actually moved. Let me check the blue's current position.\nThe blue was at rows 40-43, cols 20-39. After 6 UPs, it should be at rows 16-19. After 1 RIGHT, it should be at cols 24-43.\nNow let me try pressing SPACE from this position to see if the animation is different.\nBut wait, I've been wasting too many actions. Let me think about what the actual goal might be.\nLooking at the current board image, the blue is now at the top of the orange area, near the magenta block. The blue is at rows 16-19, cols 24-43 (approximately). The magenta block is at rows 4-7, cols 36-39.\nThe blue's column range (24-43) overlaps with the magenta block's column range (36-39). The blue is positioned above the yellow structures.\nLet me try pressing SPACE from this position to see if the animation shows something different.\nActually, I realize I need to fundamentally rethink this game. Let me look at the SPACE animation more carefully. The animation shows:\n1. The magenta block grows vertically (converting orange to magenta)\n2. The magenta block grows horizontally (converting orange to magenta)\n3. The yellow structures are converted to magenta\n4. The gray bar at the 